From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: VyOS LS1046A maintainers <ask20@vyos-ls1046a-build>
Date: Mon, 23 Jun 2026 03:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] nf_flow_table_offload: add rate-limited diagnostics for
 silent offload failures

The flow_offload_work_add() path can silently fail in two places:

  1. nf_flow_offload_alloc() returns -ENOMEM when the flow-rule allocation
     fails — no log emitted, the flow stays SW-only silently.
  2. flow_offload_rule_add() returns -ENOENT when zero block_cb drivers
     accepted the flow (the block_cb list is empty, or every driver's
     REPLACE handler returned an error) — no log emitted.

This was diagnosed as the root cause of ASK2 C6 (issue #C6 in the RC
analysis of 2026-06-23): nf_flow_table never delivers FLOW_CLS_REPLACE to
ask.ko during iperf3 because the offload promotion silently fails before
reaching the block_cb callback.  Without diagnostics, the operator has
zero visibility into whether conntrack is even attempting offload.

This patch adds pr_warn_ratelimited() calls at both failure points so the
kernel log records the failure reason.  The rate-limiting gate is 1
message per second (the system-wide ratelimit default), so a flood of
offload failures (e.g., every SYN packet from conntrack promote) does not
spam the log.

No functional change — the non-offloaded fast-path is unchanged.
---
diff --git a/net/netfilter/nf_flow_table_offload.c b/net/netfilter/nf_flow_table_offload.c
--- a/net/netfilter/nf_flow_table_offload.c
+++ b/net/netfilter/nf_flow_table_offload.c
@@ -974,8 +974,11 @@ static void flow_offload_work_add(struct flow_offload_work *offload)
 	int err;
 
 	err = nf_flow_offload_alloc(offload, flow_rule);
-	if (err < 0)
+	if (err < 0) {
+		pr_warn_ratelimited("nf_flow_table: offload alloc failed: %d "
+				    "(flow may stay SW-only)\n", err);
 		return;
+	}
 
 	err = flow_offload_rule_add(offload, flow_rule);
 	if (err < 0)
@@ -985,6 +988,18 @@ static void flow_offload_work_add(struct flow_offload_work *offload)
 
 out:
 	nf_flow_offload_destroy(flow_rule);
+
+	/*
+	 * flow_offload_rule_add() returns -ENOENT when zero block_cb
+	 * drivers accepted the flow (no block_cb registered, or every
+	 * driver's REPLACE handler returned an error).  Log this so the
+	 * operator can distinguish "no offload backend loaded" from
+	 * "backend loaded but rejecting flows."
+	 */
+	if (err < 0)
+		pr_warn_ratelimited("nf_flow_table: offload rule-add failed: %d "
+				    "(no driver accepted the flow; check that "
+				    "an offload backend is loaded)\n", err);
 }
 
 static void flow_offload_work_del(struct flow_offload_work *offload)
